  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IACHR Special Rapporteur Freedom of  Expression within OAS - IACHR/OSR 2015-2017 - Inter-American Comission on Human Rights 2015-2017</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Specialrapport&#xf6;ren f&#xf6;r yttrandefrihet inom OAS 2015-2017    -</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Specialrapport&#xf6;ren f&#xf6;r yttrandefrihet under OAS, IACHR/OSR, bildades 1997 med syfte att stimulera medvetenheten om betydelsen av att ansvariga akt&#xf6;rer i OAS medlemsstater bidrar till att respektera och att st&#xe4;rka yttrandefriheten. Medlemsstaterna ska uppmuntras att vidta &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder som f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrar de nationella villkoren f&#xf6;r yttrandefrihet. M&#xe5;len med insatsen Yttrandefrihet i Amerika 2015-2017 &#xe4;r att fr&#xe4;mja yttrandefrihetsrelaterade r&#xe4;ttigheter i 15 medlemsl&#xe4;nder med fokus p&#xe5; Mexico, Guatemala, Colombia och Karibien.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Special Rapporteur for Freedom of Expression under the OAS, IACHR / OSR, formed in 1997 with the aim of stimulating awareness of the importance of responsible actors in OAS Member States, contributes to respect and strengthen freedom of expression. The Member States should be encouraged to take measures to improve the national conditions for freedom of expression. The aim of the intervention Freedom of Expression in the Americas 2015-2017 is to promote freedom of expression and related rights in 15 countries with a focus on Mexico, Guatemala, Colombia and the Caribbean.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective is to improve the defence and protection of the right to freedom of expression and access to information in the Americas. The overall objective will be reached through the following objectives/outcomes:
1. Increased access to international justice for journalists and victims of violations of the right to freedom of expression and to freedom of expression related to other rights, to reduce impunity regarding the crimes and to disseminate Inter-american standards on this matter.
2. Established standards regarding the promotion of rights of excluded and discriminated groups in mass media, including women.
3. Established standards and guidelines for the implementation of public policies to ensure and promote the realization of the right to freedom of expresson and access to information for children and adolecents.
4. Better understanding and better protection of the right to access to environmental information promoted among judges, lawyers, public officials and CSO.
5. Recommendations and lessons learned disseminated among judges, lawyers, public officials, and CSO on the exercise of the Right of Access to Information regarding cases of discrimination and Access to Justice.</narrative>
  </description>
